  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- Reviewer thinks this may be the best version of the song they've heard [6]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Ween - 02 - Strap On That Jammy Pack**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [7]\n- **Ween - 03 - She Wanted To Leave**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [7]\n- **Ween - 04 - Push th' Little Daisies**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [7]\n- **Ween - 05 - Now I'm Freaking Out**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [7]\n- **Ween - 06 - With My Own Bare Hands**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [7]\n- **Ween - 07 - Fat Lenny**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [7]\n- **Ween - 08 - Dr Rock**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [7]\n- **Ween - 09 - Mister, Would You Please Help My Pony**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [7]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **ween2016-04-16.mk6.nbox-platinum** (recommended): source not stated; 29 songs; 148 min; rated 4.2/5 by 5 [1]. Said about its sound: A audience member nearby sings along very loudly, and the singing is clearly audible on the recording; The recording has some audible crowd noise [4][6]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Stage talk about: Ween - 01 - [1]\n- Reviewer Nico was introduced to the taper, Nicky, at the show by Gonzo; Nicky said he'd post the recording [5]\n- Reviewer asks about a recording of the 4/15/16 show, calling it probably the best Ween show they've seen [3]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **ween2016-04-16.mk6.nbox-platinum**: taped by Nicky C; transferred by larrysellers; source: Schoeps MK6(c) -> nbox-platinum -> pcm-m10 [1]\n\n## Art and photos\n\n- Poster by Worthpoint: [ween poster Terminal 5 | #3872683182](https://www.worthpoint.com/worthopedia/ween-poster-terminal-3872683182) [8]",
